00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.760
Making your proposal.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.400
After small talk, and then&nbsp;
reluctantly opening negotiations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.800
it is time to tell people what you actually want.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.080
We were hoping to interest you in taking&nbsp;
1,000 garden gnomes for your range.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.400
To be honest, we don’t have a&nbsp;
big margin on these products.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:48.560
However, we would be willing to offer them to you&nbsp;
at a unit price of £5. What are your thoughts?”

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.400
Okay, let's just have a quick look&nbsp;
at the language that was used:&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.680
To be honest - this is language that&nbsp;
shows that you are being authentic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.760
vulnerable, transparent, trustworthy.
We would be willing - this language makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:10.560
it sound like you’re doing your buyer a favour.
What are your thoughts? Throw them the ball.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.640
You’ve made your proposal, now it’s&nbsp;
time for them to make the next move.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.160
Step and language must-have number 4

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.160
Keep calm.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.120
You’ve made your offer, and you might start&nbsp;
to worry that what you’ve offered is too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:33.280
expensive. British negotiators keep calm. Always.&nbsp;
Because keeping calm influences the language that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:39.840
you choose to use. So, as a response to your&nbsp;
proposal, you might hear one of these replies:

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.400
The coded speech.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.200
I think they’re worth every penny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.720
but it might be challenging for us&nbsp;
to pay that much from our budget.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.200
The understatement.
 &nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:59.120
Interesting, but that price wasn’t&nbsp;
quite what we were expecting.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.080
Humour, aka the comedian. 
That gnome you’ve brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.840
with you is looking at me and&nbsp;
asking me to buy it for £3

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.440
The vague approach - aka the philosopher.&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.080
I’ve never really thought about how&nbsp;
much a garden gnome costs to produce.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.080
All four of these responses are saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:29.120
the exact same thing. There is no way on earth&nbsp;
that we are paying £5 for one garden gnome!

